From 80815f2187322371b7fb7c3a92c60df687fdd8d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:57:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Parameters of the behaviour variables in device code

Each device compatible behaviour class declares a structure holding the
values of its parameters and of the parameters of its behaviour variables,
recursively (mfront_parameters_values). It is filled on the host from the
parameters initializers (mfront_get_parameters_values) and applied in
device code (mfront_set_parameters_values), including to the behaviour
variables created by factories.

The parameters structure of the generic-parallel interface derives from
it: the types of the parameters are no longer duplicated, and a parameter
of a behaviour variable changed on the host is no longer refused.

The BehaviourVariableTest test changes a parameter of its behaviour
variable through a parameters file and compares the results on the device
with the ones of the generic interface.
